A credential variable referenced anywhere but the curl capture is refused,
however the command is spelled: a leading redirection, an assignment
prefix, a pipeline. A leading redirection does not hide an environment dump
either.
-- rules-alert.yml --
name: rules-alert
on: workflow_dispatch
permissions: {issues: write}
jobs:
  alert:
    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04
    steps:
      - env: {PO_USER: "${{ secrets.PUSHOVER_USER_KEY }}"}
        run: |
          >&2 echo "$PO_USER"
          X=1 printf '%s' "${PO_USER}"
          u=$PO_USER; true
          2>/dev/null env
          FOO=1 printenv
          r=$(curl -sS --form-string "user=$PO_USER" https://api.pushover.net/1/messages.json)
          echo "$r" | jq -e '.status == 1' >/dev/null
-- want --
rules-alert.yml:10 secret-output
rules-alert.yml:11 secret-output
rules-alert.yml:12 secret-output
rules-alert.yml:13 secret-output
rules-alert.yml:14 secret-output
